        "caption_cL7P9r": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "YES WE CAN",
            "text_style": "caption-with-letter-spacing",
            "text_size": "medium"
          }
        },
        "heading_Ywdkjg": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "2009. Two riders get cut loose from a program that wanted them to follow the rules. Instead of quitting, they started their own brand. No shareholders, no committee, no one who'd never stood on a board telling them how to build one.",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_yhQBQY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>That's YES. Built from a middle finger to corporate snowboarding and a stubborn belief that the sport should be run by the people who actually ride it. For over a decade we've built boards the way riders want them built, not the way a spreadsheet says they should be built.</p><p>Along the way we've had partners. We've had backers. We've sat through boardrooms and budget meetings with people who'd never stood on a board telling us how to build one. None of that stuck. What stuck was the riding.</p><p>2026: we bought ourselves back. #YES is independent again, same riders, same reason we started this in the first place. Snowboarding should always be rider-driven, not boardroom-driven.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "caption_cL7P9r",
        "heading_Ywdkjg",
        "text_yhQBQY"
